    Why docker?
Docker is more light weight and provides the same functionality as a virtual machine.
    Virtual Machines                             Docker
1)Occupies alot of memory space              Docker containers occupy less space on the host machine
on the host machine.
2)Long boot-up time                          Short boot-up time.
3)Running multiple virtual machines          Containers have a better performance as they
leads to unstable performance                are hosted in a single Docker engine.
4)Difficult to scale up                      Easy to scale up.
5)Low efficiency                             High efficiency
6)Compatibility issues while porting         Easy portable across different platforms
across different platforms
7)Data volumes cannot be shared              Data volumes can be shared and reused among multiple containers

DevOps and its tools
    What is DevOps
This is a collaboration between development and operation teams which enables continuous delivery of applications and services to our end users.
Developers are interested in
-Planning
-Codebase
-Building
-Testing
while Operations are to efficiently
-Deploy
-Operate
-Monitor
For planning and codebase, we use tools like git or jira
For Building, we use Gradel and Maven
For Testing we use Selenuim(Se)
The integration between dev and ops, we use Jenkins
The deployment Operation is done with Docker and chef
For Monitoring, we use Nagios

    What is Docker?
Docker is a tool which is used to automate the deployment of applications in lightweight containers so
that the applications can work efficiently in different environments.
The container is a software package that consist with dependecies requred to run the application.
    Docker container Features
-Multiple containers run on the same hardware
-The containers are Maintained in isolated environment
-They are highly productive
-They are quick and easy to configure
Example
1)lets take an example where you plan to rent a house in Airbnb
But in the house, there are 3 rooms and only one cupboard and kitchen.
-Problem: non of the guest wants to share cupboard and kitchen.
Because every individual has different peferences when it comes to the cupboard and kitchen usage
-solution: we put a kitchen and cupboard in eachroom
2)lets use the example with computers, where all the three applications use different frameworks
What if i want to run all my applications with their suitable frameworks?
This is where docker will help you run the applications with their different frameworks
solution: Docker provides the suitable frameworks for each suitable application
Since Every Appllication has a framework with a suitable version,
this space also can be utilized for a new software application along with its required framework.

How does Docker work
Docker is the base engine installed on your host machine to build and run containers using docker components and services.
-Docker uses a client-server architecture
There is a client installed on the hardware and
there is a client that conatins the docker product.
there is a server that controls how the docker client is created
-Docker client and server communicate using Rest Api
-Docker client is a service which runs a command
The command is translated using REST API and is sent to the Docker Daemon(Server)
-Then, Docker Daemon checks the client request and interacts with the operating system in order to create or manage containers

What are the components of Docker?
The four main components the comprises the docker engine
1)Docker client and server
2)Docker images
3)Docker containers
4)Docker registry

Docker client and server
-Docker client is accessed from the terminal(power shell) and docker Host runs the Docker Daemon and registry
-A user can build Docker images and run Docker containers by passing commands from the Docker client to Docker Server

Docker images
-Docker image is a template with instructions, which is used for creating Docker containers.
-A Docker image is built using a file called Docker file
-once you have created that file, the docker image is stored in a Docker Hub or in a repository(like registry.hub.Docker.com)
    Syntax to create a Docker Container using Docker image
Docker container create [OPTIONS] IMAGE [COMMAND] [ARG]
-you are creating an option of a new container
-you are identifying what the image will look like
-what are the commands needed and the arguements in those commands

Docker containers
-The Docker container is a standalone executable software package which includes applications and their dependecies.
-Docker is so light weight that Numerous Docker Containers run on the same infrastructure and share operating system(os) with its other container.
-Here, each application runs in isolation

Docker registry
Docker registry is an open source server-side service used for hosting and distributing images.
-Docker also has its own default registry called Docker Hub
-Here, images can be stored in either public or private repositories.
public repositories can be used to host Docker images which can be used by everyone.
private repositories allows a user to store Docker images that he/she wants to keep priavte.
-Pull and push are the commands used by users in order to intreact with a Docker registry
In order to build a container, pull command is used to get a Docker image from the Docker repository
    syntax
Docker pull <image_name>:<tags associated with the image>
This pulls an image from Docker Repository
-With push command, a user can store the Docker image in Docker registry
    syntax
Docker push <image_name>:<tag>
This pushes an image to Docker Repository

Recap
-Docker file creates a Docker image using the build command
-A docker image contains all the docker project's code
-Using the Docker image, any user can run the code in order to create Docker Containers
-once a Docker image is built, its uploaded in a registry or a Docker Hub which can be shared across your entire team
-From the Docker Hub, users can get the Docker image and build new containers

Video 2
What is docker
This is a way to package software so it can run on any hardware.
Three things you must know to understand how the process works
-Dockerfile: This is a blue print for building a docker image.
-Image: This is a template for running a docker container
-Container: This is a running process
The developer that created the software can define the environment with a docker file
Then any developer can use the docker file rebuild the environment which is saved as an imutable snapshot know as an image
Images can be uploaded to the cloud and be made both public and private registries
And any developer that wants to run that software can pull the image down to create a container(which is just the running process of that image)
In other words, one image file can be used spon the same process multiple times in multiple places
    Steps
Download docker extensions for your IDE
The dockerfile conatains code to build the docker image and ultimately run your app as a container
-create a docker file in the project
    Docker commands
docker ps
This gives a list of all the running containers on your system

